# Everything is stored and checked out with LF, on every operating system. A .sh file checked out
# with CRLF fails on Ubuntu with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", a .tsv checked out with CRLF
# carries a \r in its last field, and PowerShell reads LF without complaint, so one rule covers
# all of them. Git applies the LAST matching pattern; the one exception stays below this line.
* text=auto eol=lf
bin/ai-core.cmd text eol=crlf
